  "7b3b674b-5fa2-43b6-968b-5cbd54672d16-103384": {
   "text": "To solve the given determinant problem, we begin by interpreting the matrix structure from the provided sequence of factorial expressions. The key is to recognize that the sequence of factorials corresponds to a 3×3 matrix. The sequence is:\n\n```\n2! 3! 2! 3! 2! 4! 0! 3! 2!\n```\n\nThis gives us **nine** elements, which fits perfectly into a 3×3 matrix. We can now assign the values as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n2! & 3! & 2! \\\\\n3! & 2! & 4! \\\\\n0! & 3! & 2!\n\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the factorials:\n\n- $2! = 2$\n- $3! = 6$\n- $4! = 24$\n- $0! = 1$\n\nSubstituting these values into the matrix gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}\n2 & 6 & 2 \\\\\n6 & 2 & 24 \\\\\n1 & 6 & 2\n\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\n---\n\nWe now compute the determinant of this 3×3 matrix using the standard cofactor expansion along the top row:\n\n$$\n\\text{det} = a(ei - fh) - b(di - fg) + c(dh - eg)\n$$\n\nAssigning:\n\n- $a = 2$, $b = 6$, $c = 2$\n- $d = 6$, $e = 2$, $f = 24$\n- $g = 1$, $h = 6$, $i = 2$\n\nNow compute each component:\n\n1. $a(ei - fh) = 2(2 \\cdot 2 - 24 \\cdot 6) = 2(4 - 144) = 2(-140) = -280$\n2. $-b(di - fg) = -6(6 \\cdot 2 - 24 \\cdot 1) = -6(12 - 24) = -6(-12) = 72$\n3. $c(dh - eg) = 2(6 \\cdot 6 - 2 \\cdot 1) = 2(36 - 2) = 2(34) = 68$\n\nAdding these together:\n\n$$\n\\text{det} = -280 + 72 + 68 = -140\n$$\n\n---\n\nThus, the determinant evaluates to **-140**, and the correct answer is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{B}\n$$",
